  "_spellbook_doc": "Four spellbook slots (Q, E, R, F; League Q W E R) hold any four known spells, from any sphere; two cantrips (1, 2; League D F); the staff strike (LMB), the Ward (hold RMB; League C) and Blink are always there (spell and combat spec section 5). Magicks are retired: their code stays until combined spells replace it, but nothing casts them.",
  "start_spellbook": ["ember_bolt", "pillar", "pebble", "pyroclasm"],
  "start_cantrips": ["kindle", "douse"],
  "_casting_doc": "Every spell has a wind-up ('cast' speed band and 'windup' seconds), a release and a recovery (spell and combat spec section 3). While winding up you move at the band's 'move'; in recovery at 'recovery_move'. Hold to wind up, release to cast: letting go early cancels with nothing spent, except a Swift spell (or any spell under smart cast), which a tap commits and which fires when its wind-up ends. Blink cancels a wind-up or recovery. A hit whose Impact is above 'focus' breaks the wind-up and costs 'interrupt_cost' of the spell's Aether; a hit at or below Focus doesn't even flinch you while you wind up.",
  "casting": {"swift": {"move": 0.7, "recovery": 0.25}, "weave": {"move": 0.4, "recovery": 0.4}, "incant": {"move": 0.0, "recovery": 0.6}, "recovery_move": 0.8, "focus": 1, "interrupt_cost": 0.5},
  "_staff_doc": "The staff strike: free, instant, every 'every' seconds; an arc ('arc' radians) 'reach' sim px in front of you; it shoves props. It exists so the gaps between spells have a verb, never to win a fight with.",
  "staff": {"reach": 24, "arc": 1.8, "damage": 3, "impact": 1, "every": 0.6, "knock": 30},
  "_ward_doc": "The Ward: hold to raise a shield arc ('arc' radians) toward the cursor. It drains 'drain' Aether a second and 'per_hit' per hit stopped; Impact 'breaks_at' or more breaks it and staggers you; out of Aether it drops. You move at 'move' while it is up.",
  "ward": {"arc": 2.4, "drain": 6, "per_hit": 8, "breaks_at": 3, "move": 0.7, "cool": 1.0},
  "_cantrips_doc": "Cantrips: instant, cheap, on 'charges' that come back every 'recharge' seconds; each has a fight use and a world use. Kindle lights lamps and sets props burning where you point and singes (and marks) enemies there; Douse puts out fire there and soaks enemies.",
  "cantrips": {
    "kindle": {"name": "Kindle", "element": "fire", "blurb": "A spark where you point: lights a lamp or hay, singes and marks an enemy.", "aether": 4, "charges": 2, "recharge": 6.0, "range": 70, "r": 8, "damage": 2, "impact": 1, "pips": 1},
    "douse": {"name": "Douse", "element": "water", "blurb": "A splash where you point: puts out a fire and soaks whoever stands in it.", "aether": 4, "charges": 2, "recharge": 6.0, "range": 70, "r": 14, "wet": 4.0}
  },
  "_aether_doc": "Aether is scarce (spell and combat spec section 4.1): a pool of 'max' pays for 3-4 real spells. In a fight it comes back at 'regen_fight' a second; out of a fight at 'regen_out' a second, but only up to 'out_cap' of the pool. Rest (waking at dawn, meditating) fills it and clears Strain. Each spell sets its own 'aether'; 'costs' is the fallback by cast band. Cadence: a spell that differs from the last one adds a note and refunds 'refund' Aether; at 'notes' notes the next spell is Resonant (size x 'resonant_size', counts + 'resonant_count'). Notes fade after 'note_life' seconds without a cast. Casting the same spell again no longer dulls it: cooldowns stop repeats.",
  "aether": {"max": 100, "regen_fight": 3, "regen_out": 15, "out_cap": 0.6, "costs": {"swift": 14, "weave": 25, "incant": 45, "magick": 50}},
  "_overdraw_doc": "Short on Aether, a spell still casts: each missing point costs 'hp_per_aether' HP and adds 'strain_per_aether' Strain. Strain lowers your max Aether one for one until you rest; an Overdraw at 'backlash_at' Strain or more stuns you for 'backlash_stun' seconds. Desperate, never efficient.",
  "overdraw": {"hp_per_aether": 1.0, "strain_per_aether": 1.0, "backlash_at": 50, "backlash_stun": 2.0},
  "cadence": {"notes": 4, "refund": 4, "note_life": 4.0, "resonant_size": 1.3, "resonant_count": 1},
  "_dodge_doc": "A circle telegraph the wizard places never lands faster than a wizard-speed target can leave it: delay >= reaction + (radius + wizard radius) / wizard speed (design/magic-world-revisit.md section 3).",
  "dodge": {"reaction": 0.25},
